  "notes": "West leads the ♥9 against 3NT. West's lead should be won in the dummy. Finessing the ♥10 is too dangerous. East may be able to win the ♥Q. The defense would likely be able to set the contract in spades.\n\nThere are 8 top tricks (2 hearts, 3 diamonds, and 3 clubs). South will succeed easily if either diamonds or clubs divide evenly. However, if neither of these suits split, South will have to fall back on the heart finesse for his ninth trick. South should unblock the ♥J at trick 1. This play will prove necessary if South later takes the heart finesse.\n\nSouth should next test diamonds and clubs. When the defense turns up with stoppers in both suits, South must fall back on the heart finesse.\n\nNotice that if South had kept the ♥J he could not succeed even with the heart finesse working. West would not cover and dummy's third heart trick would be stranded.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♥9 against 3NT. West's lead should be won in the dummy. Finessing the ♥10 is too dangerous. East may be able to win the ♥Q. The defense would likely be able to set the contract in spades.",
